    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in **Gunnar Henderson**, who anchors the lineup with a stellar 83.29 score. Facing the soft-tossing Miles Mikolas, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 17% SP skill boost and a favorable platoon advantage that makes him the premier start of the day. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Josh Lowe** (72.21) are high-ceiling plays against Brandon Young and Roki Sasaki, respectively; both hitters benefit from aggressive matchup metrics and elevated park factors that push them into elite territory. We are leaning heavily into these high-efficiency profiles to capitalize on the weak opposing rotations.\n\nThe most difficult decision at the margins was excluding **Sam Antonacci** from the starting nine. Despite an elite xwOBA of 0.400, **Sam Antonacci** (54.41) fell just short of the threshold, largely due to a \"Wind In\" penalty that hampered his projected power output against Colin Rea. While the optimizer favored the defensive versatility and recent form of **Dominic Smith** (54.84), **Sam Antonacci** remains our top emergency option should any last-minute lineup shuffles occur. Meanwhile, **Jackson Merrill** (56.83) and **Andy Pages** (57.18) are currently slotted in despite the presence of formidable arms like George Kirby and Grayson Rodriguez; their high-leverage order positions provide just enough floor to justify their inclusion over bench candidates like **Coby Mayo** or **Josh Jung**. \n\nA critical risk factor today is the \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board, which forces us to rely on historical order projections. We are monitoring weather reports closely, as any shift in wind patterns could immediately devalue hitters like **Nolan Schanuel** (61.46) or **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (65.59), the latter of whom remains a strong play despite a slight platoon drag against Jack Flaherty. With SB scarcity remaining our primary strategic constraint, we are prioritizing the high-upside speed profiles inherent in our top-tier starters to ensure we maximize our 5x5 footprint before game caps become a limiting factor later in the week.",
